    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you compare the thermal conductivity and heat dissipation rates of ceramic vs semi-metallic brake pads during heavy braking cycles? specifically looking at how they handle heat soak in high-performance applications.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ceramic brake pads typically have lower thermal conductivity compared to semi-metallic brake pads, meaning they can handle heat buildup better during prolonged or heavy braking, which helps to minimize heat soak. Semi-metallic brake pads, due to their metal content, have higher thermal conductivity, providing quicker dissipation and cooler temperatures during heavy braking. However, in high-performance applications, the choice between them depends on the need for consistent pad life, feel, and braking force vs. the importance of immediate heat management. Ceramic pads offer smoother and quieter braking with less dust and longer lifespan, while semi-metallic pads offer strong, consistent performance with however much heat absorption.",
